      "value": "@{60f7dac8160e9525fc0b3102|full_name} I mean, you already can do it with HTTP Get which would results in your IP Address being leaked anyway if you had Untrusted URL set to Allowed.\n\nI think as a compromise if security is a concern, we could have world being required to inform the user of the risks, which URL needed to be allowed, and the reasons why such URL is required for expanded feature of the world. Though I think it would probably means needing a different feature request to have per-world option of \"Allow Untrusted Url\" toggle or we could call it \"Allow Untrusted Websocket Url\" toggle.\n\nIf user's consent to allowing untrusted URL is not sufficient, then VRChat could also mandate code signing certificate or requiring additional documentations from creators for extended API access if it's something that VRChat feels strongly about and with that would contains many levels of verification and liability for the creators that will hold them accountable.\n\nOn my end, I'm willing to go through the hoops to get it rolling if it means bringing my vision to reality.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
